  "summary": "The study compares pristine Ti3C2Tx, an Ar-annealed Ti3C2Tx control, and three urea-annealed N\u2212Ti3C2Tx variants prepared at 350, 400, and 450 \u00b0C. It also fabricates a MnO2\u2212CNTs (1:1) non-MXene counter/reference electrode for Zn-ion hybrid-device testing. N\u2212Ti3C2Tx\u2212350 \u00b0C is the headline material, delivering 390 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4; it has 1.33 nm interlayer spacing and 19.5 m2 g\u22121 BET area. Pristine Ti3C2Tx reached an explicitly reported 212 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 for Zn2+ storage in 1 M ZnSO4. Numerical capacitances for A-Ti3C2Tx and the 400/450 \u00b0C variants were referenced in Table S1 but were not included in the supplied paper text."
}